          "source_id": "never_callout_compile_context_gap",
          "origin": "review-1",
          "kind": "configuration",
          "change_ids": [
            "g0022",
            "g0023"
          ],
          "requirement": "Exercise compilation of a pattern containing (?C) with PCRE2_EXTRA_NEVER_CALLOUT set in the compile context.",
          "target_route": "The fuzzer already passes input-derived patterns and a compile context to pcre2_compile. Setting the supported extra option on that context before the same compile call would reach the changed rejection branch.",
          "failure_condition": "The context retains its default extra_options value of zero, so no fuzz input can make the NEVER_CALLOUT guard true or exercise acceptance of that extra option by the compile-option mask.",
          "alternative_paths": "A pattern can supply (?C), but neither the pattern-start options nor the tracked inline extra options set NEVER_CALLOUT. The harness's match callout is configured in a different context after compilation and is not an equivalent route.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [
        {
